Subject: Give Foundation's Testing stub a workspace-unique module name

swift-corelibs-foundation carries a minimal Testing module solely to satisfy
SwiftPM's generated test runner without importing the toolchain Foundation.
In a multi-root Swift Build workspace, that private stub otherwise writes
Testing.swiftmodule into the shared products directory and shadows the real
toolchain Testing module for unrelated packages.

Sentinel: NUCLEUS_FOUNDATION_UNIQUE_TESTING_STUB_MODULE

diff --git a/Package.swift b/Package.swift
index c0ad41358..36b97ad46 100644
--- a/Package.swift
+++ b/Package.swift
@@ -324,8 +324,9 @@ let package = Package(
             ],
             path: "Sources/XCTest"
         ),
+        // NUCLEUS_FOUNDATION_UNIQUE_TESTING_STUB_MODULE
         .target(
-            name: "Testing",
+            name: "FoundationTestingStub",
             dependencies: [],
             path: "Sources/Testing"
         ),
@@ -336,7 +337,7 @@ let package = Package(
                 "FoundationXML",
                 "FoundationNetworking",
                 "XCTest",
-                "Testing",
+                "FoundationTestingStub",
                 .target(name: "xdgTestHelper", condition: .when(platforms: [.linux, .android, .windows]))
             ],
             resources: [
